  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following complex ions has electrons that are symmetrically filled in both <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> orbitals?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xg06k",
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e8n7Z",
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oOlzH",
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dIq7Y",
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Metal ion having either&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;configuration&nbsp;can be filled symmetrically in both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;orbitals.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;configuration,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;configuration.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;configuration but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>CN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is strong field ligand and it will pair the electrons due to which electronic configuration is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mn>5</mn></msup><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub><mn>0</mn></msup></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" height=\"127\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/image21-0d1b3aa4-287e-470d-af50-f53f3b0bc373.jpg\" width=\"406\" /></p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>&nbsp;is weak field ligand hence&nbsp;back pairing of electrons do not take place or in case of weak field ligand pairing energy of electrons (P )is greater than crystal field splitting energy in octahedral complex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>o</mi></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;i.e.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>o</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;, hence electrons will go in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;orbitals,&nbsp;instead of back paired in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;orbitals.</p></blockquote>",
